  "body": "## Dependency and scope\n\nDepends on draft #350 at `aac15a69e9bc2e6de01652282d9da4012a0af067`.\nReview order: #331 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #334 \u2192 #340 \u2192 #343 \u2192 #347 \u2192 #350 \u2192 this PR.\nStaging #344 remains a sibling after #343. No merge or production activation.\n\nPlaceToPay previously derived inbox IDs from raw JSON, permitting repeated query\ntriggers by varying unsigned fields or formatting. After original-body signature\nverification, the handler and store now derive a versioned identity from the\nsigned request/status/date/signature tuple. Signature hex casing is normalized;\nthe existing database unique key provides concurrency deduplication.\n\n- Ignore unsigned/formatting/caller-ID variations; preserve distinct signed tuples.\n- Reject the untrusted-store bypass for PlaceToPay.\n- Preserve immutable metadata/trust/resource checks and terminal processing state.\n- Keep exact legacy redelivery on its original ID/UUID/ciphertext, including the\n  prior uppercase-signature minimal projection.\n- Leave PayPal/PayPhone IDs, external provider references, API DTOs and generated\n  web/mobile clients unchanged. No new migration, dependency or capability activation.\n\n## Verified local evidence\n\nFinal code/test commit: `f93a70f1e3740685dceb70e757caead562dbd7d6`.\nmacOS / Stack lts-24.42 / GHC 9.10.3; disposable PostgreSQL 16; Node 24.8.0.\n\n- Baseline: 112 provider-focused examples, zero failures.\n- Provider-focused increment: 118 examples, zero failures on `93ae918b76a54db4700f0331aa8b8bcf568b7deb`.\n- Full final backend: **2,589 examples, zero failures**.\n- Final real PostgreSQL callback/retry suite: **45 examples, zero failures**, including\n  nine new concurrency/legacy/handler cases. The handler test calls the Servant\n  handler directly, not a listening HTTP server or provider sandbox.\n- Existing migration repeat-apply/rollback/refusal/reapply test: passed.\n- Catalog gate: 1,413 files / 1,122 candidates / zero unreviewed; no gate or decision changes.\n- Both disposable test containers were confirmed removed. Whitespace and new local\n  documentation links checked. Existing compiler warnings were not suppressed.\n\nThe focused suite overlaps the full suite. All provider payloads/credentials are\nsynthetic; mocks are not sandbox success. No screenshots, browser/native-device,\nprovider sandbox, staging payment, live transaction or production deployment is claimed.\nExact commands, timestamps, diagnostic failure and commit mapping are in\n`docs/payments/notification-identity-2026-09-14.md`.\n\n## Compatibility and operational limits\n\nA reformatted pre-upgrade notification may create one additional canonical query\ntrigger; subsequent variations converge. Historical duplicates/ciphertext are\nnot rewritten or purged. This is a bounded forward fix, not retroactive cleanup.\nNever infer another payment from another callback row. All writers must be upgraded\nfor the new guarantee; old writers can still amplify raw-body IDs.\n\nOfficial PlaceToPay docs say session callbacks are not retried. Durable acceptance\nand reconciliation remain necessary. Account SHA-256 activation must be verified;\nrecurring notifications using `internalReference` are not implemented here.\nRollback is code-only with provider entry points disabled; preserve all evidence\nand reconcile outstanding sessions. Reverting the writer loses the new guarantee.\n\nStaging health endpoints returned 200, but six hosting metadata/secret-name reads\nreported `hosting_authentication_unavailable`. No deployed version, merchant\naccount or provider credentials were qualified. Restore app-scoped hosting auth,\nqualify sandboxes and register callbacks before activation. Staging #344 CI is\ngreen; that is not staging payment evidence. Parent #350 backend was still running\nat the last recorded check; this PR's hosted results are pending.\n\nArchitecture, official sources, threat controls and rollback:\n`docs/adr/0118-signed-payment-notification-identity.md`.\nRemaining settlement, recurring, refund/void and compliant marketplace/legal/PCI\nwork remains explicitly open. This does not complete the broader payment platform.\n",
